Capture desktop frames at the rate asked, and say what a capture costs

The next capture waited the whole interval after the last one ended, so a
capture that took 20 ms made 30 frames a second into 19, and on a slow
computer far fewer. It is now due one interval after the last one began
(at once when that is already past, never several to catch up). Screens are
no longer compared frame by frame for an updated region nobody reads. Every
10 s, WebRTC's log says at the info level how many captures were made and
what one cost.

diff --git a/src/rtc_desktop_capturer_impl.cc b/src/rtc_desktop_capturer_impl.cc
